            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Domestic Policy and the \"Jamahiriya\" System</strong><br>\nGaddafi introduced the \"Jamahiriya,\" or \"state of the masses,\" in Libya, which he claimed was a form of direct democracy, though in practice it was considered authoritarian, with power concentrated in his hands.</p>\n\n<p><strong>c1</strong><br>\nEarly Life and Political Rise</p>\n\n<p><strong>Kim Jong-il was born on February 16, 1941, and began his political career in the ruling Workers' Party of Korea, eventually being groomed for succession by his father, Kim Il-sung. He held key positions in the party and military, consolidating power before his father's death.</strong><br>\nLeadership Transition</p>\n"
              },
